[
  {
    "role": "paragraph",
    "segment": "Prescriptive process models describe how to perform the process to meet goals or standards, while descriptive process models describe how the process is actually carried out in practice and can be described in flexible ways that allow people to design and build software using preferred techniques and tools.",
    "citations": [
      {
        "type": "source_text",
        "content": "A process is a collection of procedures, organized so that we build products to satisfy a set of goals or standards.",
        "img_id": null
      },
      {
        "type": "source_text",
        "content": "a software development process can be described in flexible ways that allow people to design and build software using  preferred  techniques  and  tools",
        "img_id": null
      }
    ],
    "type": null
  },
  {
    "role": "paragraph",
    "segment": "The purpose of a descriptive model is to reflect how the process actually operates in practice and to capture organizational factors and flexibility, whereas the purpose of a prescriptive model is to guide actions toward achieving specified goals or standards and to enforce structure when needed.",
    "citations": [
      {
        "type": "source_text",
        "content": "The process structure guides our actions by allowing us to examine, understand, control, and improve the activities that comprise the process.",
        "img_id": null
      },
      {
        "type": "source_text",
        "content": "The process may suggest that we choose from several procedures, as long as the goal we are addressing is met.",
        "img_id": null
      }
    ],
    "type": null
  },
  {
    "role": "paragraph",
    "segment": "When to use each: use descriptive models to understand how a process is actually performed in a given context and to study factors influencing behavior; use prescriptive models to impose consistency, achieve standard goals, or guide improvement when a defined approach is required.",
    "citations": [
      {
        "type": "source_text",
        "content": "A process is a collection of procedures, organized so that we build products to satisfy a set of goals or standards.",
        "img_id": null
      }
    ],
    "type": null
  }
]

