  {
    "role": "paragraph",
    "segment": "To describe getting a degree as a work breakdown structure, treat the degree process as a set of activities each with four parameters: the precursor, duration, due date, and endpoint. In other words, for each activity, specify what must precede it, how long it takes, when it should be completed, and what the completion looks like (the endpoint).",
    "citations": [
      {
        "type": "source_text",
        "content": "We can describe each activity with four parameters: the precursor, duration, due date, and endpoint.",
        "img_id": null
      }
      ,
      {
        "type": "source_text",
        "content": "the nodes of the graph are the project milestones, and the lines linking the nodes represent the activities involved.",
        "img_id": null
      }
    ],
    "type": null
  },
  {
    "role": "paragraph",
    "segment": "The critical path is the sequence of activities that determines the project end date. If the critical path has no slack, there is no margin for error when performing the activities along its route. Delays on the critical path propagate and can push subsequent activities late.",
    "citations": [
