[
    {
        "role": "paragraph",
        "segment": "A comprehensive requirements-definition template developed by James and Suzanne Robertson can be found at the Web site of the Atlantic Systems Guild: http:// www.systemsguild.com. This template is accompanied by a description of the Volere process model, which is a complete process for eliciting and checking a set of requirements.",
        "citations": [
            {
                "type": "source_text",
                "content": "A comprehensive  requirements-definition  template  developed  by  James  and Suzanne Robertson can be found at the Web site of the Atlantic Systems Guild: http:// www.systemsguild.com.This template is accompanied by a description of the Volere process model, which is a complete process for eliciting and checking a set of requirements.",
                "img_id": null
            }
        ],
        "type": null
    },
    {
        "role": "paragraph",
        "segment": "Our criteria for validating the requirements are the characteristics that we listed in Section 4.4: - Correct - Consistent - Unambiguous - Complete - Relevant - Testable - Traceable. Depending on the definition techniques that we use, some of the above checks (e.g., that the requirements are consistent or are traceable) may be automated.",
        "citations": [
            {
                "type": "source_text",
                "content": "Requirements Validation Our criteria for validating the requirements are the characteristics that we listed in Section 4.4: - Correct - Consistent - Unambiguous - Complete - Relevant - Testable - Traceable",
                "img_id": null
            },
            {
                "type": "source_text",
                "content": "Depending on the definition techniques that we use, some of the above checks (e.g., that the requirements are consistent or are traceable) may be automated.",
                "img_id": null
            }
        ],
        "type": null
    },
    {
        "role": "paragraph",
        "segment": "Validation checks can be performed by simple means such as reading the document and reporting errors, and common errors can be recorded in a checklist, which reviewers can use to guide their search for errors.",
        "citations": [
            {
                "type": "source_text",
                "content": "Table 4.3 lists some of the techniques that can be used to validate the requirements. Validation can be as simple as reading the document and reporting errors. We",
                "img_id": null
            },
            {
                "type": "source_text",
                "content": "However, most validation checks (e.g., that a requirement is correct,relevant,or unambiguous;or that the requirements are complete) are subjective exercises in that they involve comparing the requirements definition against the stakeholders' mental model of what they expect the system to do. For these validation checks, our only recourse is to rely on the stakeholders' assessment of our documents.",
                "img_id": null
            },
            {
                "type": "source_text",
                "content": "Also,common errors can be recorded in a checklist , which reviewers can use to guide their search for errors.",
                "img_id": null
            }
        ],
        "type": null
    },
    {
        "role": "paragraph",
        "segment": "The Robertson template is described as a comprehensive requirements-definition template and is associated with a complete validation/checking process (Volere). It supports validation by providing defined characteristics to verify and by offering a checklist-based approach to identify errors.",
        "citations": [
            {
                "type": "source_text",
                "content": "A comprehensive  requirements-definition  template  developed  by  James  and Suzanne Robertson can be found at the Web site of the Atlantic Systems Guild: http:// www.systemsguild.com.This template is accompanied by a description of the Volere process model, which is a complete process for eliciting and checking a set of requirements.",
                "img_id": null
            },
            {
                "type": "source_text",
                "content": "Validation can be as simple as reading the document and reporting errors.",
                "img_id": null
            }
        ],
        "type": null
    }
