    {
        "role": "bullet",
        "segment": "Possible steps drawn from the text to promote egoless behavior include using a diverse review audience aligned to different reader classes, focusing discussions on detecting faults early, and keeping the review group small to facilitate open discussion.",
        "citations": [
            {
                "type": "source_text",
                "content": "In an active design review (Parnas  and Weiss 1985)  is  a  particularly  effective method for evaluating the quality of the SAD and determining whether it contains the right information. In an active review, reviewers exercise the design document by using it in ways that developers will use the final document in practice.",
