    {
        "role": "paragraph",
        "segment": "Design patterns are not the same as software libraries; they are not packaged solutions that can be used as is. Rather, they are templates for a solution that must be modified and adapted for each particular use. The main goal of design patterns is to improve a design's modularity. In fact, each pattern is designed to encapsulate a particular type of design decision. The original design patterns identified by Gamma et al. (1995) are listed in Table 6.4, along with the purpose of each. Let us look at some of the popular patterns in more detail. Also, this chapter includes a section titled 'Template Method Pattern' to explore at least one pattern in more detail.",
