      {
        "type": "source_text",
        "content": "AECL began with a failure modes and effects analysis to identify single failures leading to significant hazards. Then, to identify multiple failures and quantify the results, it performed a fault-tree analysis. Finally, it hired an outside consultant to perform detailed code inspections of the software functions related to the most serious hazards: electron-beam scanning, energy selection, beam shutoff, and dose calibration.",
        "img_id": null
