[
  {
    "role": "paragraph",
    "segment": "Object-Oriented encapsulation and information hiding support reuse by structuring software around interfaces and well-defined responsibilities: each class encapsulates the implementation details of one or more interfaces, and each interface is implemented by one or more classes. An advantage of object composition is its support of modularity, the composite class knows nothing about the implementations of its object-based attributes and can manipulate these attributes only by using their interfaces. As such, we can easily replace one class component with another, as long as the replacement complies with the same interface. Support for reuse is a key characteristic of OO design.",
    "citations": [
      {
        "type": "source_text",
        "content": "Each class encapsulates the implementation details of one or more interfaces.",
        "img_id": null
      },
      {
        "type": "source_text",
