    ],
    "type": null
  },
  {
    "role": "paragraph",
    "segment": "Differences from conventional testing are highlighted by cautions from Beizer and the described limitations: cleanroom’s lack of unit testing promotes dangerous malpractice, contradicting 'known testing theory and common sense' and 'you cannot find a bug unless you execute the code that has the bug,' while orthodox cleanroom relies only on statistical testing to verify reliability, shunning unit testing of any kind. Moreover, statistical usage testing itself can be misleading. Beizer points out that cleanroom is never measured against proper unit testing, testing done by software engineers trained in testing techniques, testing performed by organizations that use test design and automated testing techniques, or proper integration testing.",
    "citations": [
      {
        "type": "source_text",
        "content": "Beizer describes the results of 24 empirical studies that have evaluated cleanroom, including Basili and Green's (1994), pointing out that they have several fatal flaws.",
        "img_id": null
      },
      {
        "type": "source_text",
        "content": "Beizer suggests that we read the results with caution. He claims that cleanroom's lack of unit testing promotes dangerous malpractice, contradicting 'known testing theory and common sense.'",
        "img_id": null
      },
      {
        "type": "source_text",
        "content": "According to Beizer,'you cannot find a bug unless you execute the code that has the bug,' and orthodox cleanroom relies only on statistical testing to verify reliability, shunning unit testing of any kind.",
        "img_id": null
      },
      {
        "type": "source_text",
        "content": "Beizer points out that cleanroom is never measured against",
        "img_id": null
      },
      {
        "type": "source_text",
        "content": "proper unit testing done by addressing coverage goals",
        "img_id": null
      },
      {
        "type": "source_text",
        "content": "testing done by software engineers trained in testing techniques",
        "img_id": null
      },
      {
        "type": "source_text",
        "content": "testing performed by organizations that use test design and automated testing techniques",
        "img_id": null
      },
      {
        "type": "source_text",
        "content": "proper integration testing",
        "img_id": null
      },
      {
        "type": "source_text",
        "content": "Beizer points out that cleanroom is never measured against proper unit testing",
        "img_id": null
      },
      {
        "type": "source_text",
